# This machine has `core.autocrlf=true` globally, which would give the working
# tree CRLF and make every file disagree with CI on Linux. `eol=lf` overrides
# autocrlf for this repo, so the checked-out bytes match the committed bytes
# match what CI sees.
#
# This matters more here than in a normal repo: shadcn-drift's whole job is
# comparing file content against a registry, and a line-ending mismatch is
# exactly the kind of false positive it exists to rule out. Its own sources
# should not be a source of that confusion.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Recorded registry payloads are compared byte-for-byte by the test suite.
# Never let git normalize them.
packages/*/test/fixtures/** -text

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
